.TH mtr-ng 1  "mtr-ng 0.4.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mtr\-ng \- A modern implementation of mtr (My Traceroute) with unicode and terminal graphics
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmtr\-ng\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-M\fR|\fB\-\-max\-hops\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-report\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-csv\fR] [\fB\-\-dot\fR] [\fB\-\-geojson\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-numeric\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-aslookup\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-geo\fR] [\fB\-\-geoip\-mmdb\fR] [\fB\-\-origin\fR] [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-mpls\fR] [\fB\-\-flows\fR] [\fB\-\-sparkline\-scale\fR] [\fB\-\-ema\-alpha\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-show\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-simulate\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-protocol\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
A modern implementation of mtr (My Traceroute) with unicode and terminal graphics
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR
Number of rounds to run (default: until quit; 10 in report mode)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 1000]
Time between rounds in milliseconds (at least 100, except with \-\-simulate)
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-max\-hops\fR \fI<MAX_HOPS>\fR [default: 30]
Maximum number of hops (1\-255)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-report\fR
Enable report mode (non\-interactive)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Report as JSON, with mtr\*(Aqs field names (implies \-\-report)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-csv\fR
Report as CSV, one row per hop (implies \-\-report)
.TP
\fB\-\-dot\fR
Print the routes as a Graphviz graph instead of a table (implies \-\-report). Most useful with \-\-flows
.TP
\fB\-\-geojson\fR
Print the located hops and the path between them as GeoJSON, for map tools (implies \-\-report; needs a geolocation database, see \-\-geo)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-numeric\fR
Show IP addresses instead of hostnames
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-aslookup\fR
Show the AS number of each hop. Asks Team Cymru\*(Aqs DNS about every public address
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-geo\fR
Show where each hop is (Location and Dist columns), from a local geolocation database: nothing is sent anywhere. A location farther away than light in fibre gets in the hop\*(Aqs best RTT is marked with !
.TP
\fB\-\-geoip\-mmdb\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Geolocation database in MaxMind\*(Aqs format: DB\-IP City Lite or GeoLite2 City. Default: the newest .mmdb in ~/.local/share/mtr\-ng, then the usual system places
.TP
\fB\-\-origin\fR \fI<LAT,LON>\fR
Where you are, in degrees, for distances and the plausibility check. Default: the first hop the database places in a city, with its uncertainty
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-mpls\fR
Show the MPLS labels routers report (RFC 4950) under their hop
.TP
\fB\-\-flows\fR \fI<FLOWS>\fR [default: 1]
Probe this many flows in turn, one per round. All probes of a flow look alike to load balancers (Paris traceroute), so a flow follows one path; several flows reveal the paths a load balancer spreads traffic over
.TP
\fB\-\-sparkline\-scale\fR \fI<SPARKLINE_SCALE>\fR [default: logarithmic]
Sparkline scaling mode: linear or logarithmic (default: logarithmic)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
linear
.IP \(bu 2
logarithmic
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ema\-alpha\fR \fI<EMA_ALPHA>\fR [default: 0.1]
Smoothing factor for the EMA column, above 0 and at most 1. Higher follows recent RTTs faster
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Select which columns to display (default: hop,host,loss,sent,last,avg,ema,best,worst,graph)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
hop: Hop number
.IP \(bu 2
host: Hostname/IP address
.IP \(bu 2
asn: Origin AS number (looked up with \-\-aslookup)
.IP \(bu 2
geo: Where the hop is, from the geolocation database (see \-\-geo)
.IP \(bu 2
dist: Distance from the origin in km (see \-\-origin)
.IP \(bu 2
reach: Farthest from here a reply can come in the best RTT, in km
.IP \(bu 2
loss: Packet loss percentage
.IP \(bu 2
sent: Number of packets sent
.IP \(bu 2
last: Last RTT measurement
.IP \(bu 2
avg: Average RTT
.IP \(bu 2
ema: Exponential moving average RTT
.IP \(bu 2
jitter: Last jitter value
.IP \(bu 2
jitter\-avg: Average jitter
.IP \(bu 2
best: Best (minimum) RTT
.IP \(bu 2
worst: Worst (maximum) RTT
.IP \(bu 2
stdev: Standard deviation of the RTT
.IP \(bu 2
graph: RTT sparkline graph
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-all\fR
Display all available columns
.TP
\fB\-\-simulate\fR
Show fake data instead of probing (for demos and testing); marked SIMULATED
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-protocol\fR \fI<PROTOCOL>\fR [default: icmp]
Probe protocol (only icmp is implemented so far)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
icmp: ICMP Echo (ping) \- default and most common
.IP \(bu 2
udp: UDP probes (not implemented yet)
.IP \(bu 2
tcp: TCP SYN probes (not implemented yet)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Report mode: print errors only, no warnings
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Append debug logs to this file (level can be overridden with RUST_LOG)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
Target hostname or IP address
